## A ten-minute onboarding checklist

This checklist expands the in-app welcome guide into concrete steps. Work through it once on macOS or iPadOS; repeat any step when you onboard a new device.

{% note %}
Shortcuts below are **macOS defaults** from the app command catalog. On iOS and iPadOS, use touch controls and the command palette where shortcuts are unavailable.
{% /note %}

## Minutes 0–2: Orient yourself

- [ ] Launch Cardmaniacs and complete iCloud setup if prompted
- [ ] Press `⌘0` to open **Home** and note recommendations and reading stats entry points
- [ ] Press `⌘⌥2` for **Triage layout**—list on one side, reader on the other (macOS)
- [ ] Press `⌘K` to open the **Command palette** and type “Go to” to see sidebar destinations

You now know the two layouts and the palette—the app's universal search for actions.

## Minutes 2–4: Add content

Choose at least one path:

- [ ] **Add a feed** — `⌘⌥N`, paste a site URL or RSS link, confirm discovery
- [ ] **Quick add a link** — `⌘N`, paste any article URL into Read Later or Bookmarks
- [ ] **Import OPML** — `⌘⇧O` if you have feeds exported from another reader

Then press `⌘R` to **refresh feeds** and wait for new articles to appear under **Feeds → Unread**.

## Minutes 4–6: Triage like a desk

- [ ] Go to **Feeds** with `⌘1`
- [ ] Select an unread article and press `⌘↩` (**Accept**) to open it in the reader
- [ ] Press `⌘E` to **mark as read** when finished, or `⌘⇧S` to **star** it for later
- [ ] Try **Archive** from the command palette (`⌘K`, type “Archive”) to clear it without deleting

{% tip %}
Star (`⌘⇧S`) is for importance within a list. **Save to Read Later** (palette) moves an item to your reading queue—a different intent.
{% /tip %}

## Minutes 6–8: Read Later queue

- [ ] Press `⌘2` for **Read Later**
- [ ] Save an article from Feeds using the actions palette (`⌘⇧A`) → **Save to Read Later**
- [ ] Open **In Progress** from the command palette to see partially read items
- [ ] Press `⌘⌥L` to return to Read Later sidebar mode anytime

Skim [Read Later](/docs/read-later) when you are ready to build queue habits.

## Minutes 8–10: Reader and extensions

- [ ] With an article open, press `⌘=` / `⌘-` to adjust **font size**
- [ ] Press `⌘⌥T` for the next **reader theme**
- [ ] Press `⌘⇧F` to toggle **focus mode** (hide chrome)
- [ ] Enable the **Share extension** in **Settings → Share** (and verify it is on in Safari or Settings.app on iOS)

Optional power moves:

- `⌃L` — **Focus cards** (keyboard focus to the list)
- `⌘⇧T` — **Manage Tags…** on the current item
- `⌘⇧A` — **Actions palette** for highlights, move, and archive

